<strong class="text-strong">vChimes</strong> is an interactive physical simulation of wind chimes. The chimes are rendered in 3d using openGL ES. How the individual chimes are connected, move, and collide with each other is simulated by the incredible open source physics library Bullet.<br><br>the Simulation is available at <a href="http://itunes.apple.com/WebObjects/MZStore.woa/wa/viewSoftware?id=311431240&amp;mt=8" class="postlink">http://itunes.apple.com/WebObjects/MZSt ... 31240&amp;mt=8</a><br><br><br>Thanks Irwin for creating such an awesome library,<br><br>Bob<dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=268" class="postimage" alt="1.jpg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=3040">SouthpawBob</a> — Tue Apr 14, 2009 6:46 pm</p><hr />
